Recommends: unitotem-node
Description: Orchestrator for UniTotem kiosks
 UniTotem plays playlists of images, videos, PDF documents and web pages on
 screens, and is managed through a web interface served over HTTPS: uploads,
 scheduling, users, backups and remote control of other nodes.
 .
 This package is complete on its own: installed alone it is a server that
 orchestrates other UniTotem nodes and touches nothing of the machine it runs
 on. What belongs to a machine with screens (network, audio, displays,
 power, timers, updates) is in unitotem-node, and the local windows are in
 unitotem-viewer.

Package: unitotem-node
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         login,
         netplan.io,
         network-manager,
         unitotem-manager (= ${source:Version}),
         x11-xserver-utils,
         python3-croniter,
         python3-packaging,
         python3-pulsectl,
         python3-qrcode,
         python3-sdbus-networkmanager,
         python3-xlib,
Recommends: alsa-utils, ddcutil, tigervnc-scraping-server, v4l-utils
Description: UniTotem integration with the machine it runs on
 Network (NetworkManager through netplan), audio, displays and screen power
 (DDC, CEC, Wake-on-LAN, serial), reboot and power-off, timers, system
 updates, a terminal and a view of the screen in the web interface and the
 hotspot of the first boot.
 .
 Install it on every machine that is a totem; leave it out of a server that
 only orchestrates.

Package: unitotem-viewer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3-cefpython3,
         python3-croniter,
